# KAGE-MAN.DOJO :: labs.manifest — the range as configuration
#
# One continuous campaign from the WAN: white-belt modules -> brown-belt
# configure/chaining/auxiliary -> black-belt manual exploitation + full MSF
# workflow -> a pivot masterclass -> the persistence capstone (msfvenom
# payloads that survive a restart and a real reboot).
#
# columns: lab_path                 ip             seg       [frontend] [pport] [extra-homes]
#   extra-homes dual-homes a container onto a second segment (the pivot seams).

# ================= WAN — the internet edge =================
# Seven exposed services; only activemq is dual-homed (the single door into
# the DMZ). The rest are attack-surface warm-ups that lead nowhere deeper.
vulhub/activemq/CVE-2023-46604       10.0.8.20      wan       activemq   61616   dmz:192.168.80.20
vulhub/struts2/s2-045                10.0.8.21      wan       struts2    8080
vulhub/spring/CVE-2022-22965         10.0.8.22      wan       spring     8080
vulhub/cacti/CVE-2022-46169          10.0.8.23      wan       web        80
vulhub/joomla/CVE-2015-8562          10.0.8.24      wan       web        80
vulhub/opensmtpd/CVE-2020-7247       10.0.8.25      wan       smtpd      25
vulhub/erlang/CVE-2025-32433         10.0.8.26      wan       sshd       2222

# ================= DMZ — reachable only through the WAN door =================
# white belt — reflex set A: data stores & servers
vulhub/couchdb/CVE-2017-12635        192.168.80.21  dmz       couchdb    5984
vulhub/redis/4-unacc                 192.168.80.22  dmz       redis      6379
